1.11.0: the zero-argument release

Every release argument was derivable, so now it derives: release.sh
defaults the repo to the sibling directory named polajuice, the tag to
v$(cat VERSION), and the message file to COMMIT_MSG_$VERSION. It also
locates its own tree, so it can be invoked by path from the parent
directory. The ritual shrinks to: untar, sh
polajuice-src/scripts/release.sh. Explicit arguments still override
everything (the e2e harness uses them), and every existing preflight
guard is unchanged.

scripts/pjdeploy is the optional one-time-install wrapper (copy to
~/bin) that collapses the ritual to a single word: it finds the newest
polajuice tarball in ~/Downloads, extracts it in the house directory,
and hands off to that tarball's own release.sh.
